eady supported. But maybe they want a test proving it. I'll add a test that CallCLI with extraArgs `--append-system-prompt <file>` produces argv with those args.)\n\nLet me now think about whether `Run` should be fully functional or a stub. The phrase \"piRuntime 骨架\" + \"接口签名仅占位，以 task8 为准\" suggests the Run signature is a placeholder that will be finalized in task8. But key result 6 also specifies concrete behaviors for Run. I'll implement Run functionally (temp file + --append-system-prompt + promptFile as user prompt + parse + return sessionID/trace), which satisfies both \"skeleton\" (not wired to handlers) and the concrete behaviors. This is the safest to pass any tests/checks.\n\nLet me now plan the actual code.\n\nFirst, let me check: does the codebase have any existing `runtime` import anywhere that would conflict? The package `internal/runtime` would be imported as `runtime`. In `internal/cmd`, is stdlib `runtime` imported? Let me check.\n\nLet me also check the cmd files that import piagent to see how they use it, and check for potential conflicts. Also check `tools_init_pi.go` and `tools_theme.go` in detail since they use many piagent functions.\n\nLet me look at cmd files that need updating.\n\nActually, let me first check for stdlib `runtime` usage in the cmd package and elsewhere.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_TrT0S0pftaLRwrYxIhVj6745","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== stdlib runtime import ===\" && grep -rn '\"runtime\"' internal/ --include='*.go' && echo \"=== check go version ===\" && go version && echo \"=== git status ===\" && git status --short && echo \"=== git log ===\" && git log --oneline -5"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_ljjqXE9cpxzrSIILWfVC9002","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== tasks.json ===\" && cat .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json 2>/dev/null | head -200"}}],"api":"openai-comp