{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"There's a test timeout in `internal/cmd` — `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_ResumesFromTasksJSON`. This test is hanging because it's invoking the real pi (parseStream is stuck reading from a real pi process that doesn't terminate, or a real pi that's hanging).\n\nWait, this is the known bug from bugs.md: \"pi 解析'托管运行时优先'后，PATH-fake 测试静默命中真实 pi（挂死/联网）\". The test `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_ResumesFromTasksJSON` probably uses a fake pi via PATH, but now the `internal/runtime` package's `Executor.Execute` resolves via `RuntimeBin()` first (managed runtime). Since the managed runtime (`~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/.bin/pi`) might exist on this machine, it hits the real pi and hangs.\n\nWait, but this test was presumably passing before my change. Let me check — actually the issue is that the cmd test `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_ResumesFromTasksJSON` might be relying on a fake pi in PATH. But now with my migration, the resolution order is the same (RuntimeBin first). So why would it hang now but not before?\n\nActually wait — this is likely a PRE-EXISTING issue. Let me check whether this test passes on the current HEAD (before my changes) by checking git. Actually, the task4.py test script only runs `go build ./...`, `go test ./internal/runtime/...`, and `go test ./internal/config/...`. It does NOT run `go test ./internal/cmd/...`. \n\nBut the task.md key result 5 says: \"`go build` + `go test ./internal/runtime/... ./internal/cmd/... -timeout 60s` 全绿\".\n\nSo I DO need `go test ./internal/cmd/... -timeout 60s` to pass. But this test is hanging. Let me investigate whether this is pre-existing or caused by my change.\n\nLet me check: the test `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_ResumesFromTasksJSON` in doing_test.go. Let me look at it. It might set up a fake pi via PATH and expects the runtime to use it. With the \"managed runtime priority\" behavior, the test needs to isolate `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR` to a temp dir so RuntimeBin doesn't hit the real managed runtime.\n\nBut wait — this is a cmd-level test, and the bug in bugs.md says tests should isolate. Let me check if this test was already passing before. Actually, the bug note says \"job_34 / commit c4812dc 验证状态: ✅ 已修复\". So the test should already isolate.\n\nHmm, but my migration might have changed something. Let me check: did I change the resolution logic? No, I copied the files verbatim (only package rename). The `Executor.Execute` and `piPathOrDefault` logic is identical.\n\nWait — actually, let me check if this test was already hanging BEFORE my change. Let me stash my changes temporarily? No, that's risky. Instead, let me look at the test and understand what it does.\n\nActually, let me first check: is the real managed runtime present on this machine?"}}
