_DIR` to a temp dir so RuntimeBin doesn't hit the real managed runtime.\n\nBut wait — this is a cmd-level test, and the bug in bugs.md says tests should isolate. Let me check if this test was already passing before. Actually, the bug note says \"job_34 / commit c4812dc 验证状态: ✅ 已修复\". So the test should already isolate.\n\nHmm, but my migration might have changed something. Let me check: did I change the resolution logic? No, I copied the files verbatim (only package rename). The `Executor.Execute` and `piPathOrDefault` logic is identical.\n\nWait — actually, let me check if this test was already hanging BEFORE my change. Let me stash my changes temporarily? No, that's risky. Instead, let me look at the test and understand what it does.\n\nActually, let me first check: is the real managed runtime present on this machine?","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_1vAeY6yfQDYCz3J9Cz991422","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== managed runtime bin ===\" && ls -la ~/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/.bin/pi 2>&1; echo \"=== RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR ===\" && echo \"$RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR\"; echo \"=== which pi ===\" && which pi 2>&1"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_pOZ2YW5x2dhrgzY1mMm82671","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/cmd/doing_test.go","offset":420,"limit":120}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1796,"output":903,"cacheRead":104832,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":691,"totalTokens":107531,"cost":{"input":0.00078126,"output":0.0007856100000000001,"cacheRead":0.000380016,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001946886}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786902497233,"responseId":"20b7d8ad-9847-4757-9780-7afe128223b9","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
