k:\n\nTest `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_ResumesFromTasksJSON`:\n- Sets HOME=temp, config.json max_retries:2.\n- Creates plan with task1, task2.\n- Pre-creates doing/tasks.json with task1=success, task2=pending.\n- Mock pi (renamed) exits 0.\n- PATH = mockDir + \":\" + origPath.\n- Calls `executeDoingWorkflow(\"job_resume\")`.\n- The workflow: creates executor with `piExec := runtime.NewExecutor(\"\")` (PiPath empty). Then executor runs task2 → invokes pi → mock pi exits 0 → no test script created → task2 fails → after retries, workflow returns error (ignored).\n- Then loads tasks.json and checks task1 still \"success\".\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety: `executeDoingWorkflow` calls `config.LoadConfig()` which reads config.json (max_retries:2). Then creates executor with MaxRetries=2. Then runs ExecuteJob. Task1 is already success (from tasks.json resume), so it skips task1. Task2 runs → mock pi exits 0 → parseStream reads empty stdout → sess with no sessionID, no settled → duration fallback. The runner then checks if the task produced a test script... Let me check what makes task2 \"fail\".\n\nActually, the comment says \"mock claude exits 0 but never creates a test script, so task2 will fail\". The task success criterion is presumably that the agent creates a test script (`.rick/jobs/.../doing/tests/task2.py`). The mock pi doesn't create it, so task2 fails. Good.\n\nBut wait — does the mock pi need to emit valid JSONL? The `parseStream` reads stdout. If mock pi exits 0 with empty stdout, `scanner.Scan()` returns false immediately (EOF), `scanner.Err()` = nil. So `parseStream` returns `sess` (empty session) and nil error. Then `Execute` returns `sess, nil`. Good, no error. Then the runner proceeds to check the test script, finds it missing, marks task2 failed. \n\nSo renaming `claude` → `pi` should work. But there's the MaxRetries issue: with MaxRetries=2, and the mock pi \"failing\" (task2 fails), it might retry a few times, but each retry is fast (mock pi exits immediately). So total time is short.\n\nActually wait, let me check: does the runner retry on task failure? `MaxRetries=2`. Each attempt invokes the mock pi (fast). So 2 attempts, fast. Then task2 fails. Good.\n\nLet me also check `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_WithMockClaude` (lines 511+). Same pattern.\n\nOK, but there's also a THIRD consideration: are there OTHER cmd tests that use `claude` mock or real pi? Let me grep the whole cmd test dir for `claude` mocks and `pi` mocks.\n\nActually, let me check ALL cmd test files for mock binaries named `claude` or referencing `claude` executable.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_npZtydOIIvtOkIW1LXuq8372","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn '\"claude\"\\|claude\\b\\|LookPath(\"pi\")\\|mock_pi\\|\"pi\"' internal/cmd/*_test.go | grep -i 'claude\\|mock.*pi\\|lookpath\\|mockdir\\|mockpath' | head -50"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":317,"output":1814,"cacheRead":119168,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1696,"totalTokens":121299,"cost":{"input":0.000137895,"output":0.00157818,"cacheRead":0.000431984,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.002148059}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786902648533,"responseId":"376e9d36-d921-42a4-a4fc-9f09b755e94e","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_npZtydOIIvtOkIW1LXuq8372","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"internal/cmd/doing_test.go:481:\t// Use a mock claude that exits 0 but never creates a test script,\ninternal/cmd/doing_test.go:485:\tmockPath := filepath.Join(mockDir, \"claude\")\ninternal/cmd/doing_test.go:493:\t// Run the workflow — it will fail on task2 (mock claude doesn't create test script),\ninternal/cmd/doing_test.go:511:// TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_WithMockClaude tests executeDoingWorkflow with mock claude\ninternal/cmd/doing_test.go:513:\t// Create mock claude that exits 0 but creates no