uccess)\n- .rick/loops/tdd-red-green-refactor-loop.md\n- Untracked: .rick/draft/loops/loop_6/, .rick/draft/rfc/..., .rick/jobs/job_32/, job_33/, job_34/, job_35/...\n\nThese are pre-existing (from the plan/dream phases of job_35 and previous jobs). I should NOT commit those (they're not part of task4's code changes).\n\nSo my commit should include ONLY:\n- internal/runtime/ (new package, all files)\n- internal/agent/piagent/ (deleted files)\n- internal/cmd/*.go (modified)\n- internal/config/*.go (modified)\n\nAnd then the tasks.json update (task4 → success + commit_hash) in a SEPARATE commit (per the mark_task_success skill).\n\nLet me NOT commit bin/rick (leave it as working-tree artifact). Actually, wait — let me reconsider. The task's \"正常路径\" says `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick && go test ./internal/runtime/...`. It's a verification step, not necessarily \"commit the binary\". The binary is a build artifact. I'll exclude it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one more time. bin/rick is tracked. If I leave it modified and don't commit, the repo will have a stale binary (the old one in HEAD) vs the new source. But that's how task1/task2 handled it (they didn't touch bin/rick). And the release commits handle binary sync. So I'll follow the same pattern: commit source only.\n\nNow, let me stage and commit the source changes.\n\nFirst, let me review the full diff of the key NEW files one more time to ensure correctness (runtime.go, executor.go isSessionReady, config). I've already reviewed them. Let me also make sure I haven't accidentally left any `piagent` string anywhere in internal/ (besides the deleted dir).\n\nLet me do the final grep check and then commit."}}
